  <uui-button id="crf-add-pool" class="orange" size="xs" onclick="crfAddPool();return false;">Add pool</uui-button>

:crf_pools_plug:
> Each pool has its own routing label, fixed target, autoscale floor, optional ceiling, idle buffer, CPU claim, and memory claim. Workflows request the generated selector directly, for example `runs-on: ci-pool-python`. Do not add `self-hosted`; that would also make the job eligible for legacy runners.
>
> Set **Max** to `auto` to admit runners from the available CPU and memory budget instead of a fixed runner count. The host resource budget remains the hard admission boundary.
>
> Saved pool IDs are immutable. To rename one, duplicate it with the new ID and routing label, save, move workflows to the new selector, then remove the old pool; removing it drains its runners as jobs finish.
:end

<div class="crfp-routing-warn" id="crf-routing-warn">Runner pools reserve routed capacity; they are not security isolation. Restrict the GitHub runner group to trusted repositories.</div>

